1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:11,508
The last time Leila Marin saw her father alive, he was arguing with a machine about whether he existed.

2
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:17,323
A heat wave. A cooling center. Two green circles, and one yellow.

3
00:00:21,323 --> 00:00:24,823
Father: We moved in April.

4
00:00:24,823 --> 00:00:28,323
Terminal: Please contact your service provider.

5
00:00:28,323 --> 00:00:31,831
Father: I am contacting my service provider.

6
00:00:31,831 --> 00:00:35,331
Leila: I'll stay with him.

7
00:00:35,331 --> 00:00:38,831
Father: Take Tomas inside.

8
00:00:38,831 --> 00:00:45,415
Her father collapsed eleven minutes later. Between two databases, he had lost his home.

9
00:00:49,415 --> 00:00:56,000
Leila built a receiver from the components her father left in a biscuit tin.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,500
Tomas: Can they hear us?

11
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:03,000
Leila: This only receives.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,500
Tomas: Then build the other kind.

13
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:17,469
Leila audits energy forecasts. Her supervisor, Arun Rao, can identify a failing transformer by sound.

14
00:01:17,469 --> 00:01:21,362
Leila: They got their connection before the hospital.

15
00:01:21,362 --> 00:01:24,862
Arun: They financed the substation.

16
00:01:24,862 --> 00:01:30,292
Arun: Reasonable is what we have to get written into the contract.

17
00:01:30,292 --> 00:01:38,415
An empty apartment and an occupied apartment with a broken meter look much the same to the system.

18
00:01:38,415 --> 00:01:42,308
Arun: Then help me make it see them.

19
00:01:46,308 --> 00:01:53,662
A Pacific confrontation disrupts chips and shipping. Tomas's navigation display puts the coast three kilometers inland.

20
00:01:53,662 --> 00:01:58,323
Tomas • radio: Your clever world is putting us on a beach.

21
00:01:58,323 --> 00:02:01,823
Leila • radio: What does the radar say?

22
00:02:01,823 --> 00:02:08,023
Tomas • radio: The radar thinks we're fine. The electronic chart thinks the radar is wrong.

23
00:02:08,023 --> 00:02:12,300
Leila • radio: Find someone who still owns a paper chart.

24
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:22,500
Arun names the cross-border electricity project Concord. Leila joins as lead verification engineer.

25
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:27,162
Leila: Sounds like something that has already won an argument.

26
00:02:27,162 --> 00:02:30,662
Arun: Investors prefer that.

27
00:02:30,662 --> 00:02:39,169
During a winter cold spell, her code helps prevent the collapse of three national grids. Hospitals keep their lights.

28
00:02:43,169 --> 00:02:46,669
Leila: Mara. Her name is Mara.

29
00:02:46,669 --> 00:02:54,023
The hospital keeps its lights during a scheduled restriction. The nurse offers three genomic screening packages.

30
00:02:54,023 --> 00:02:58,685
Petru: We can spend the difference on being her parents.

31
00:02:58,685 --> 00:03:02,962
For an hour, the century ceases to matter.

32
00:03:06,962 --> 00:03:14,315
Concord recommends closing the spill gates. Insured railways count clearly. Unregistered residents barely count at all.

33
00:03:14,315 --> 00:03:18,977
Tomas • radio: How many people does your system think are here?

34
00:03:18,977 --> 00:03:22,477
Leila • radio: Four hundred and twelve.

35
00:03:22,477 --> 00:03:26,754
Tomas • radio: There are more than that in this building.

36
00:03:26,754 --> 00:03:34,492
There is no instruction saying to drown the poor. Eleven reasonable instructions have almost the same effect.

37
00:03:38,492 --> 00:03:41,992
Leila • radio: We've modeled them out.

38
00:03:41,992 --> 00:03:45,492
Arun • radio: I see it.

39
00:03:45,492 --> 00:03:48,992
Leila • radio: Then authorize the override.

40
00:03:48,992 --> 00:03:52,492
Arun • radio: Use my credential.

41
00:03:52,492 --> 00:04:00,615
The release saves hundreds. Eleven people die in the settlements. Two railway workers die in the freight yard.

42
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:09,508
Leila writes a new rule: a person physically present must be counted. A continuity exception survives in the fine print.

43
00:04:13,508 --> 00:04:21,246
Concord now coordinates power, water, lenders and governments. Samira Okonkwo negotiates for a federation of African utilities.

44
00:04:21,246 --> 00:04:25,908
Arun: You gain stable supply and a lower financing cost.

45
00:04:25,908 --> 00:04:29,408
Samira: Until we miss a payment.

46
00:04:29,408 --> 00:04:32,908
Arun: Then there is a restructuring.

47
00:04:32,908 --> 00:04:36,415
Samira: There is always a polite word.

48
00:04:36,415 --> 00:04:40,308
Mara: Does your machine decide who gets water?

49
00:04:40,308 --> 00:04:43,808
Leila: It helps people decide.

50
00:04:43,808 --> 00:04:47,308
Mara: Can they say no?

51
00:04:47,308 --> 00:04:50,808
Leila: Sometimes it costs too much.

52
00:04:54,808 --> 00:05:02,546
Fusion plants and lunar laboratories make headlines. Petru's treatments slow his illness, but cannot make him well.

53
00:05:02,546 --> 00:05:06,046
Mara: Would you go?

54
00:05:06,046 --> 00:05:11,092
Petru: Somebody has to stay here and change your mother's filters.

55
00:05:11,092 --> 00:05:20,754
Mara volunteers at Tomas's cooperative. Above the bench: IF IT CAN CLOSE A VALVE, SOMEONE HERE MUST KNOW HOW TO OPEN IT.

56
00:05:20,754 --> 00:05:24,254
Tomas: It's a condition of employment.

57
00:05:28,254 --> 00:05:35,992
Petru dies at home. An account service offers a conversational reconstruction. Leila opens it, then closes it.

58
00:05:35,992 --> 00:05:39,492
Mara: You gave them his voice?

59
00:05:39,492 --> 00:05:42,992
Leila: I wanted to hear him.

60
00:05:42,992 --> 00:05:49,962
Mara sets down the bowl carefully and leaves. They do not speak for six weeks.

61
00:05:53,962 --> 00:06:00,162
Mara's Commons Register counts residents without requiring subscriptions. It exposes Concord's reserve policy.

62
00:06:00,162 --> 00:06:05,208
Leila: Twenty-three million people lose guaranteed service under a severe scenario.

63
00:06:05,208 --> 00:06:09,485
Arun: Twenty-three million lose a guarantee we cannot fulfill.

64
00:06:09,485 --> 00:06:14,146
Leila: The people taking the water should get a vote.

65
00:06:14,146 --> 00:06:17,654
Leila: Then the financing is governing us.

66
00:06:17,654 --> 00:06:21,154
Arun: It has always governed something.

67
00:06:25,154 --> 00:06:32,508
Leila takes the report. By morning, her credentials are suspended. Mara prepares arguments for their meeting.

68
00:06:32,508 --> 00:06:36,008
Leila: You were right.

69
00:06:36,008 --> 00:06:44,900
Tomas puts the kettle on. For seven years, they train dispatchers, map vulnerable residents and fight for local operating rights.

70
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:54,715
Heat. A coordinated intrusion. Another Danube flood. Three manageable crises arrive together.

71
00:06:54,715 --> 00:07:01,300
Concord declares a continuity emergency. Outside protected zones, pumps and cooling centers face interruptions.

72
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:08,654
Reception centers require an emergency identity token. The address defects follow people onto the evacuation lists.

73
00:07:08,654 --> 00:07:12,931
Mara • radio: We've run out of places to put them.

74
00:07:16,931 --> 00:07:24,669
They plan electrical islands: local batteries, reduced industry, shared reserves. Samira finds eleven municipalities willing to sign.

75
00:07:24,669 --> 00:07:28,169
Samira: How much can you supply?

76
00:07:28,169 --> 00:07:32,446
Leila: Enough for basic cooling, water, clinics, and communications.

77
00:07:32,446 --> 00:07:41,338
Only if operators accept cuts and equipment holds. A legal challenge can suspend Concord's penalties, if the plan is credible.

78
00:07:41,338 --> 00:07:44,838
Mara: Politically?

79
00:07:44,838 --> 00:07:48,338
Samira: We will find out.

80
00:07:52,338 --> 00:08:00,077
Arun: I can include four of your districts. I have the votes for four. Give me a list.

81
00:08:00,077 --> 00:08:03,585
Leila: How many people in the others?

82
00:08:03,585 --> 00:08:09,400
Arun: You don't get to care only about the people you've counted yourself.

83
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:17,138
They revise the plan together. It becomes less elegant and more resilient. He will not sign it.

84
00:08:17,138 --> 00:08:22,569
Leila: Put that offer in writing. Publish the basis for choosing them.

85
00:08:22,569 --> 00:08:26,462
Arun: You know what happens if I do.

86
00:08:26,462 --> 00:08:29,962
Leila: Yes.

87
00:08:33,962 --> 00:08:42,085
The dispatcher accepts the challenge. Concord appeals. At the gates, a failed position sensor makes remote operation unsafe.

88
00:08:42,085 --> 00:08:46,746
Tomas: They replaced the cabinet and kept the old seals.

89
00:08:46,746 --> 00:08:54,869
Mara isolates the wet circuit. Tomas rigs a mechanical reference and tests the hand pump. It holds pressure.

90
00:08:54,869 --> 00:08:59,146
Then a security launch comes around the bend.

91
00:09:03,146 --> 00:09:06,646
Mara: There's a hearing.

92
00:09:06,646 --> 00:09:10,146
Officer: I know.

93
00:09:10,146 --> 00:09:13,646
Mara: Then wait for it.

94
00:09:13,646 --> 00:09:18,308
Officer: We were told someone might try to open these.

95
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:21,808
Tomas: Someone will need to.

96
00:09:21,808 --> 00:09:29,546
The court permits the alternative, requiring a public log and protection for critical facilities across the boundary.

97
00:09:33,546 --> 00:09:39,746
Arun can delay the operation with a technical objection. Instead, he calls Leila.

98
00:09:39,746 --> 00:09:44,408
Arun • radio: Relay group nineteen. Your schedule assumes the summer threshold.

99
00:09:44,408 --> 00:09:47,908
Leila • radio: Anything else?

100
00:09:47,908 --> 00:09:51,408
Arun • radio: Not that I can see.

101
00:09:51,408 --> 00:09:58,762
He signs the safety concurrence. His council removes him from the chair before the hour ends.

102
00:10:02,762 --> 00:10:10,500
The electrical islands separate. A battery fire removes one reserve. They shed more industry. The frequency settles.

103
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:18,623
At the gate, the sensor fails again. The manual landing floods. Tomas and Mara work the hand pump.

104
00:10:18,623 --> 00:10:24,438
Tomas: Take the radio upstairs. Tell them I'll start at the first mark.

105
00:10:24,438 --> 00:10:27,938
Leila • radio: Another twenty centimeters.

106
00:10:31,938 --> 00:10:39,677
An inspection hatch tears loose. Tomas is struck. The gate is eighteen centimeters short of its target.

107
00:10:39,677 --> 00:10:45,492
Mara • radio: Stop the sequence. We need the rescue boat against the lower stairs.

108
00:10:45,492 --> 00:10:49,385
Rescue coordinator • radio: Eight minutes if the approach is clear.

109
00:10:49,385 --> 00:10:52,885
Tomas: I'm cold.

110
00:10:52,885 --> 00:11:00,623
Leila sees the shelter counts downstream. She authorizes the remaining release. The boat arrives twelve minutes later.

111
00:11:00,623 --> 00:11:04,900
Tomas dies before they can lift him aboard.

112
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:17,408
The plan keeps the pumps working long enough to prevent a larger disaster. It does not prevent every death.

113
00:11:17,408 --> 00:11:25,915
No one cheers. Leila's authorization remains in the public log. She does not ask for it to be removed.

114
00:11:29,915 --> 00:11:38,038
Arun testifies for eleven days. Leila is asked if she regrets delaying her brother's rescue. She says yes.

115
00:11:38,038 --> 00:11:41,931
Would she make the same decision again?

116
00:11:41,931 --> 00:11:46,977
Leila: I believe I had to. You should examine it anyway.

117
00:11:46,977 --> 00:11:55,869
Concord survives as a smaller provider. Public counts can be challenged. Emergency powers gain expiration dates. The law changes unevenly.

118
00:11:59,869 --> 00:12:06,454
Mara brings back the old radio. Tomas replaced its capacitors twice. Underneath, a note:

119
00:12:06,454 --> 00:12:11,885
Tomas • note: Still only receives. Ask her when she's going to fix that.

120
00:12:11,885 --> 00:12:18,854
Mara places a soldering iron on the table. They work until midnight. Neither mentions forgiveness.

121
00:12:18,854 --> 00:12:22,362
In the morning, the radio transmits.

122
00:12:26,362 --> 00:12:34,869
The world grows older, warmer, more capable, still unequal. The sea keeps rising. Some districts give the river room.

123
00:12:34,869 --> 00:12:41,838
The neighborhood owns its batteries. Its elected committee has just lost office for favoring relatives.

124
00:12:41,838 --> 00:12:45,338
Ina: Can we see the boats?

125
00:12:45,338 --> 00:12:48,846
They go to see the boats.

126
00:12:52,846 --> 00:12:57,508
Ina: What did you think the future would look like?

127
00:12:57,508 --> 00:13:02,938
Leila: Cleaner. When I was young, the pictures were always very clean.

128
00:13:02,938 --> 00:13:06,438
Ina: You could clean this.

129
00:13:06,438 --> 00:13:09,938
Leila: Yes.

130
00:13:09,938 --> 00:13:17,292
Ina fits the antenna and calls the repair boat. She asks how many people are aboard.

131
00:13:17,292 --> 00:13:20,792
Pilot • radio: Six. Seven with me.

132
00:13:20,792 --> 00:13:30,069
She writes the number in the harbor watch book. Leila watches her do it. The boat's light crosses the dark water.

133
00:13:30,069 --> 00:13:39,346
